Z||000003||Shaun41178||01-24-2001||06:05 PM||||I have all these exact same parts that I have been trying to get rid of for some time.  All are the same except I have sealed power rings instead of the Hastings rings.  I also have the flexplate and harmonic balancer and the whole assembly has been precision balanced.  I have been looking to get rid of this assembly for about 3 months now but all I get is the price is too steep from forum members.  Seems to me my price is a good one considering what these guys are selling. From me you get the crank, pistons, rings, rods, flexplate and harmonic balancer.  All these parts have been balanced too which cost me $200.  It seems to me that the kit here that they are selling isn't balanced so add that into your cost plus the new flexplate and one will be over the $600 I am asking.<P>You can have your old block machined to fit these pistons I have as they are .030 overbore or one can buy the block that I had machined for these pistons and assembly.  price for the block is $300.  Good deal I think since it has been machined and is ready to have an assembly installed in it.  I have posts in the Mall about what I am selling if anyone cares to get more info about it.  It is still for sale too.  If anyone is interested then let me know.<P>------------------<BR>Shaun 85 GT with nitrous<BR>0-60 in 5.6 seconds<BR><A HREF="http://members.aol.com/Shaun41178" TARGET=_blank>Preferred Performance</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-24-2001||08:58 PM||||I would stay away form these guys. The prices for those stroker kits are steep for what you get and like Shaun41178 said it doesn't say if the assembly was balanced, which is a must with a stroker engine. Federal Mogul pistons are JUNK. Silvolite and Keith Black make much better quality pistons for the money. Get the parts yourself, use your 2.8 rods, find a good used 3.1 crank, and have the assembly balanced yourself and you will save money.||||reg||1
